Description: Unofficial Proton Drive client (FUSE mount, Nautilus, Dolphin and COSMIC Files integration)
 PDrive for Linux mounts Proton Drive as a FUSE file system, with on-demand
 download, offline pinning, sync state emblems and menu entries in Nautilus and
 Dolphin, entries in the sidebar and menus of Dolphin and COSMIC Files, a
 desktop application (tray icon, status window) that runs the daemon, and a
 command-line tool.
 .
 The plugins of a file manager are only loaded by it, so none is required and
 several desktops can be installed side by side.
 .
 The session is stored through the Secret Service API: the desktop must provide
 a Secret Service (oo7, GNOME Keyring, KWallet, KeePassXC...). None is pulled in
 as a dependency, so that the one already chosen by the desktop is kept.
 .
 This is an unofficial third-party client, not affiliated with or endorsed by
 Proton AG. It bundles the Proton Drive SDK and Proton cryptography libraries
 (MIT) as private libraries.
